          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ready to Go Beyond",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.798,
            0.237,
            0.938,
            0.591
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Viruses, viroids, and prions are acellular (no cells) infectious agents that are too small to be seen under a light microscope. Viruses are composed of some genetic material with a protein coat. Viroids lack protein coat around its genetic material, while prions are misfolded proteins which lack genetic material."
            }
          ]
